{"availability":"available","full":"ratulb/tenmo","name":"tenmo","description":"A fast, lean and high performance Tensor library in Mojo🔥","category":"Other","language":"Mojo","stars":16,"forks":7,"created":"2025-04-22T18:07:53Z","updated":"2026-10-14T08:34:28Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ratulb.github.io/tenmo/","topics":[],"demo":"https://ratulb.github.io/tenmo/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:08.379Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:08.379Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:08.379Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.287Z","stars":16,"forks":7},{"at":"2026-10-17T07:10:08.379Z","stars":16,"forks":7}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A light tensor library and neural network framework in Mojo — from SIMD kernels to transformers.","Tenmo provides modern, ergonomic ML abstractions with automatic differentiation, modular neural networks, and end-to-end training pipelines: MLPs and CNNs, a GPT-2-style decoder stack with text generation, and a BERT encoder for classification and masked-language modeling.","Development status. Tenmo is under active development alongside the Mojo toolchain. The API may change between releases; pin a commit for reproducible work. The library is past the experiments stage — core autograd, the transformer stacks, and training loops are covered by extensive pinned test suites — but it is not yet production-hardened."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ratulb/tenmo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"94a40cf129570f8b6d212dcb550f050b504c2d81d57402b99fc58035f5a107f8","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.383Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.383Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A light tensor library and neural network framework in Mojo — from SIMD kernels to transformers.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ratulb/tenmo/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"94a40cf1295